AI REVENUE MODELS: SHORT VERSION

WHAT IT IS
The method an AI business uses to earn money from its products, services, or infrastructure.

MAIN MODELS
1. Per-API-call: Pay per request to the AI service. Best for developers and chatbots.
2. Per-seat: Fixed fee per user (e.g., ₹1,000 x 20 users = ₹20,000/month). Best for workplace and team tools.
3. Freemium: Free tier, with paid upgrades for more features or usage. Best for consumer apps and image generators.
4. SaaS subscription: Recurring monthly or annual plans. Best for writing, CRM, and analytics tools.
5. Token-based: Pay by tokens processed (input and output). Best for LLM APIs and document processing.
6. Marketplace: Platform takes a commission on sales between buyers and sellers. Best for agent directories and plugin stores.

Models can be combined, e.g., a free tier plus subscriptions plus per-seat team pricing.

API ECONOMICS
- Gross profit = Revenue - Delivery costs
- Gross margin (%) = (Gross profit / Revenue) x 100
- Example: ₹1,00,000 revenue - ₹30,000 costs = ₹70,000 profit, a 70% margin.

If you charge ₹500 per customer but spend ₹700 on AI usage, you lose money on every customer.

Ways to fix it:
- Use cheaper models
- Cut token usage
- Cache results
- Set usage limits
- Adjust pricing
- Route simple tasks to smaller models

KEY METRICS
- MRR / ARR: Monthly / annual recurring revenue
- CAC: Cost to acquire a customer
- LTV: Value a customer generates over time
- Churn: Rate of customers leaving
- Conversion rate: Free users who become paying
- Gross margin: Revenue left after delivery costs
- ARPU: Average revenue per user

TAKEAWAY
A good AI product needs a sustainable business model, not just a good model. The right pricing depends on customers, usage patterns, value, competition, and delivery costs. High usage doesn't automatically mean high profit.
